! DECIMAL VFL ADD, LOAD AND STORE -- G2.3 stage 1, built 2026-11-16.
!
! Every expected value below is HAND-DERIVED from the Reference Manual
! 22-6530-2 (printed N = PDF N+3), read in the page images, and from
! C22-6578 printed p.15; none was taken from a run.  After each operation
! the indicator register is copied with TI (TRANSMIT IMMEDIATE, count
! one; it sets no arithmetic indicator) to Ik, and THEN the accumulator
! words 8, 9, 10 ($L, $R, $SB) are stored to Xk, Xk+1, Xk+2 with binary
! ST and L (which change the indicators, already saved).  (The first
! version wrote "T, 1, ..." -- whose 1 names INDEX REGISTER 1 as the
! count, not a count of one -- and transmitted the mask register and
! onward over Ik+1 until the step cap.  A deck error, not a model one.)  Indicator word bits (bit n of the register
! is 1 << (63-n)): LC 0x20000000000, PF 0x10000000000, TF 0x10000000,
! MOP 0x100, RLZ 0x80, RZ 0x40, RGZ 0x20, RN 0x10.  The sign byte
! register's sign bit is IBM bit 4 of word 10: 0x0800000000000000.
!
! A1-A5 ARE printed p.60's five ADD examples, IBM's own, exactly as
! printed: "ADD, L (376+) offset 8 bits (2 bytes) where acc. contains
! 75679+" -> 113279+ RGZ; (532-) on 45623+ -> 7577- RLZ RN; (532-) on
! 53200+ -> 00000+ RZ; (532+) on 53200- -> "00000-  Result zero  Result
! negative"; (532-) on 53201+ -> 00001+ RGZ.  Signed fields at byte size
! four: digits, then the sign byte S T U V (S = 8 for minus).
!
! A6  LC: 32 nines plus one.  p.60, Lost Carry: "if information is lost
!     because a carry attempts to propagate beyond the left end of the
!     accumulator."  The sum is zero, positive: RZ.
! A7  PF: 9876 at offset 120 -- digits 30-33, two of them past the left
!     end.  p.60, PF: "significant bits of the data field from storage
!     overlap the left end ... the high-order bits of the result are
!     dropped.  A partial field condition will not cause a lost carry
!     indication."  76 lands in digits 30-31 over the 12 already there.
! A8  offset 9 is offset 8: p.60, "the two low-order bits of the
!     effective offset are ignored and considered zero".
! A9  byte size 6, zones 11 on every byte: p.58, "only the four low-order
!     bits of each byte take part in the operation."
! A10 +MG, negative result: p.60, "If the result is negative, the entire
!     accumulator is cleared to zero.  In either case, the content of the
!     accumulator sign byte register is not changed."  |45623| - 53200 <
!     0: zero, sign still minus -> RZ RN (as A4).
! A11 +MG, positive: |75679| - 53200 = 22479, the sign byte still minus.
! A12 "-" is + with the negative sign modifier (p.60's Programming
!     Notes): 45623 - 37600 = 8023.
! A13 a storage sign byte 0100 (S=0, T=1): TF on (p.60, "set according to
!     the flag bits of the storage operand").
! A14 C22-6578 printed p.15, Problem 2.3 Method 4 comment (b): "The byte
!     (1 1 1 1)2, for instance, will become (0101)2 with a carry to the
!     higher byte."  L(DU) of 3F -> 45.
! A15 decimal L, PF: the digits of A7 loaded at offset 120.
!
! M1  M+, p.61: "The accumulator field specified by the offset is
!     algebraically added to the addressed operand"; acc 37600+, offset 8
!     -> 376 + 75679 = 76055+, MOP RGZ.
! M2  LC, p.62: "actuated by a carry beyond the leftmost digit ... of the
!     addressed field": 999 + 376 = 1375 -> 375 stored.
! M3  p.62: "This indicator is also turned on if the result of an
!     unsigned operation is negative.  In such a case, the magnitude of
!     the result is stored": 123 - 376 = -253, 253 stored, LC, RLZ RN.
! M4  PF, p.62: "non-zero digits ... in the accumulator to the left of the
!     highest order digit that is participating": acc 12345, a two-digit
!     field takes 45; 11 + 45 = 56.
! M5  byte size 8: p.61, "The high-order bits of each byte are not changed
!     by the operation" -- zones F kept, 12 + 34 = 46 -> F4F6.
! M6  M+1, p.63 ("identical to an ADD TO MEMORY in which the accumulator
!     operand is +1"): 99 + 1 = 100 -> 00, LC, RZ.
! M7  M-1, p.63: "if it is one, a minus one is added": 0+ - 1 = 1-, the
!     sign bit stored, digits 01, sign byte 1000.
! M8  M+MG, p.62: "If the sum is of opposite sign, zero bytes replace the
!     numeric part of the storage field.  In either case the sign byte ...
!     is not changed"; storage 375-, acc 500+: sum 125+ -> 000-.  (Figure
!     13: storage 3-, accumulator 5+, Add Magnitude to Memory -> 0-.)
!     Indicators "according to the final result stored": RZ RN.
!
! S1  signed ST, byte size 4, p.63: the sign byte from the register, S=1.
! S2  signed ST, byte size 6: three numeric bytes 00dddd and the sign byte
!     Z Z S T U V = 00 1000 (zones from the register, which are zero):
!     000110 000111 001001 001000 = 187248; PF, digits 7 and 5 are left
!     of the high-order byte stored.
! R1  decimal SRD, p.64: "a four-bit byte with value five is added to the
!     four-bit byte immediately to the right of the offset": 12345 + 5 at
!     digit 0, field from digit 1 -> 1235, three digits stored, 235; PF
!     from the digit 1 left of them.
! R2  9995 + 5 = 10000 -> 000 stored, LC (p.64: "the rounding process
!     causes a carry to be propagated beyond the left end of the field
!     stored"), and no PF: unrounded, 999 fits.
! R3  signed: 7577- rounds to 758, two digits 58 and the sign byte 1000.
! R4  offset 2 is digit offset 0, "equivalent to a STORE" (p.64): 77, PF.
!
! MEASURED INJECTIONS, 2026-11-16, each in a separate copy of bsv/ (the
! worktree's source was never touched; the copies were diffed against it
! first, one file differing in each), rebuilt and run on this deck:
!   1. mkDecBox never recomplements (rl_add's "if (rg_sub[0] && c == 0)"
!      made "if (False)"): FAILS A2_acc (0x9999999999992423), M3_field,
!      M7_field -- exactly the three subtractions with no end carry --
!      and, in run_decbox_test.sh, vectors 1 and 7; Problem 2.3 Method 4
!      stays green (it never subtracts).  67 pass, 3 fail here.
!   2. decimal RN off on a zero result (setResultIndicatorsDec's RN made
!      -- that function is setResultIndicatorsF since 2026-11-16, shared
!      with the binary arms; the injection is the same line there --
!      "sign && !zero", the binary rule): FAILS A4_ind_RZ_RN (0x40),
!      A10_ind (0x40), M8_ind (0x140) -- the three negative zeros.
!   3. decMergeField starts from zero (zones not kept): FAILS
!      M5_field_zones_kept only (0x0406FF..., zones 1111 lost) -- the only
!      M+ case whose field has byte size over four.

